    "updated_at": "2018-03-19T03:37:53Z",
    "body": "> we should move to a model where each HTML element interface is associated with exactly one constructor. \r\n\r\nI'm not quire sure I follow.  Nothing prevents writing this:\r\n\r\n    class A extends HTMLButtonElement {}\r\n    class B extends HTMLButtonElement {}\r\n\r\nand then registering A and B for two different custom element names, as far as I can tell.  That associates the `HTMLButtonElement` interface with two different constructors (`A` and `B`), no?\r\n\r\nSimilarly for things extending `HTMLElement`; presumably we do (and want to!) allow multiple different constructors to do that...",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
