    "created_at": "2018-04-26T19:58:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-04-26T19:58:19Z",
    "body": "The thing to keep in mind here is that this isn't the \"built-in element constructor binding API\". It's the custom element definition API.\r\n\r\nIf we wanted to create some separate API for changing the meaning of `new HTMLElement()` or `new HTMLQuoteElement()` or `new HTMLDivElement()`, we could do that. (Currently people seem stalled on #896 in that regard.) But it shouldn't be mixed up with custom elements, and it shouldn't have weird side effects like changing how the resulting elements interact with `:defined`, or causing them to call any custom element callbacks you've stuffed onto `HTMLElement.prototype`.\r\n\r\n> Why do I have to define a custom constructor of some sort if I just want to create `<div>`'s by constructor instead of being able to do:\r\n\r\nI think the incantation of using `customElements.define` with a div constructor \"extending itself\" is not an intuitive way to enable creating divs by constructor, and we should not allow it.\r\n\r\n> Instances defined in terms of instanceof?\r\n\r\nNo, defined in terms of what constructor was used to create them. (Roughly `.constructor`.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
